## Design

L06 layers a small ownership registry over the existing per-file mutation queue from issue #167. The registry answers a single question: which owner currently has verifiable write attribution for a path?

Ownership installation is a synchronous compare-and-set operation over a path-keyed map. The first owner receives an unguessable token. Re-claiming by that owner is idempotent and returns the existing token. A different owner receives an explicit conflict and the current holder; no contender token is issued.

